# Hand-run requests against the Oncade TEST API.
# Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above each request.
#
# Secrets are read from .env in this folder ({{$dotenv ...}}), so no key is ever
# typed into this file. Only edit @invoiceId below.

@base = https://www.oncade.gg/api/v1/platform
@key = {{$dotenv ONCADE_API_KEY}}
@business = {{$dotenv ONCADE_BUSINESS_ID}}
@invoiceId = paste-oncade-invoice-id-here

### 0a. Connection check: confirms the key works and shows "businessId"
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
X-Oncade-API-Version: v1

### 0b. Business readiness: is the business set up to receive money (payout wallet, etc.)?
# NOTE: this path comes from a summary of the docs and is not yet confirmed. A 404 means it's wrong.
GET {{base}}/business/readiness
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
X-Oncade-API-Version: v1
X-Target-Business-Id: {{business}}

### 1. Update test: look at the invoice BEFORE the change
GET {{base}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
X-Oncade-API-Version: v1
X-Target-Business-Id: {{business}}

### 2. Update test: change the amount from $1 to $2 (the FULL invoice must be sent again)
PUT {{base}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
X-Oncade-API-Version: v1
X-Target-Business-Id: {{business}}
Idempotency-Key: update-test-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "receiverName": "Gene Test",
  "receiverEmail": "me+test@gmail.com",
  "date": "2026-11-26T00:00:00.000Z",
  "payToTarget": "BUSINESS",
  "items": [
    { "description": "Update test (changed)", "quantity": 1, "rate": 2, "amount": 2 }
  ]
}

### 3. Update test: look at the invoice AFTER the change
GET {{base}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
X-Oncade-API-Version: v1
X-Target-Business-Id: {{business}}
